## Reproduction

The mutation is saved as `mutation-remove-post-await-recheck.patch` in this
folder. It was generated from commit `6cc420f` with:

```sh
git format-patch -1 6cc420f --stdout \
  > docs/04-testing/evidence/reviewer-concurrency-2026-11-06/mutation-remove-post-await-recheck.patch
```

`git apply --check mutation-remove-post-await-recheck.patch` passed on the
submission tree. To reproduce without keeping the mutant:

```sh
git switch -c bt3-mutation-repro 9264d7f
git apply docs/04-testing/evidence/reviewer-concurrency-2026-11-06/mutation-remove-post-await-recheck.patch
npx vitest run tests/unit/review-workflow.test.ts --reporter=verbose
git restore src/presets/review.ts
git switch feat/85-reviewer-concurrency
git branch -D bt3-mutation-repro
```

Expected: the unit run exits 1 with T10 failing and the other 15 tests passing.

## Result summary (from the output above)

- Failing test: T10 "a concurrent submit and approval leave a consistent revision".
  Assertion: expected 'approved' to be 'pending'.
- Unit suite: 1 failed | 15 passed (16). EXIT=1.
- Load harness: passed (p95 957.856 ms, final version 40), but it does not
  restore the safety property; the mutant is rejected on the unit result.
- Mutant killed: YES — killed **only by T10**. The raw unit output shows T07
  and T09 passing.
- T07 still passes because the pre-await `target.version !== version` check
  rejects the stale approval before the digest/await; the removed post-await
  checks are never reached on that path.
- T09 still passes because the post-await `current.status !== 'pending'` check
  remains; the mutation removes only the post-await version/contentHash
  comparisons, so the second approval is still refused as `not-reviewable`.

These explanations describe the code path; the measured claim is only the raw
test output above: 1 failed (T10) | 15 passed.

